I’m continuing work on my modular Hyprland configuration.

Environment
Hyprland: 0.56.2
Hyprland commit: efb50993780079460b0cbed1363e2166a2de1d9f
Hyprutils: 0.14.x
Hyprgraphics: 0.5.x
Hyprcursor: 0.1.x
Hyprlang: 0.6.8
Configuration uses Hyprland's Lua configuration API, not legacy hyprland.conf syntax.

Before proposing or finalizing any Hyprland-specific option, dispatcher, Lua API, plugin option, or animation feature, check the current Hyprland 0.56.x documentation/source. Do not invent syntax.

Current modular structure
~/.config/hypr/
├── hyprland.lua
└── lua/
    ├── appearance.lua
    ├── animations.lua
    ├── input.lua
    ├── plugins.lua
    └── keybinds/
        ├── init.lua
        ├── apps.lua
        ├── window.lua
        ├── navigation.lua
        ├── workspace.lua
        ├── layout.lua
        ├── mouse.lua
        └── media.lua


Responsibilities should remain separated.

appearance.lua

Owns:

rounding
blur
shadows
glow
opacity
wobble
other visual/decorative configuration
Matugen colors
animations.lua

Owns only native Hyprland animations:

animation curves
window open/close
window movement
fading
workspace transitions
layer transitions
border/shadow/glow animation

Do not put plugin configuration here.

plugins.lua

Owns Hyprland plugins.

Currently installed/enabled:

hyprfocus by Vaxry
Version: 1.0
Description: Flashfocus for Hyprland


hyprpm list reports:

hyprfocus
enabled: true


hyprctl plugins list confirms it is loaded.

Current working plugins.lua:

local M = {}

function M.setup()
	hl.config({
		plugin = {
			hyprfocus = {
				keyboard_focus_animation = "shrink",
				mouse_focus_animation = "flash",
				animate_floating = true,
			},
		},
	})
end

return M


This has been verified with:

hyprctl reload
hyprctl configerrors


and there are no errors.

These values currently report:

plugin:hyprfocus:keyboard_focus_animation
str: shrink
set: true

plugin:hyprfocus:mouse_focus_animation
str: flash
set: true

plugin:hyprfocus:animate_floating
bool: true
set: true


Do NOT try to use the old unsupported nested Hyprfocus configuration such as:

flash = {
	flash_opacity = ...
}

shrink = {
	shrink_percentage = ...
}


unless the installed plugin version is first verified to support those options.

Also:

type(hl.plugin)
→ table

type(hl.plugin.hyprfocus)
→ nil


This is not necessarily an error; the installed plugin does not expose a Lua namespace there.

Current native animations goal

I want a polished, futuristic, visually interesting desktop.

Animations do NOT need to be Niri-inspired.

Use native Hyprland animation features where possible.

Desired effects:

smooth window opening
distinctive window closing
spring-like movement/resizing where appropriate
smooth workspace transitions
subtle layer/Rofi animations
border/glow transitions
tasteful—not excessive—motion
no fake or unsupported animation options

A previous animation design used native styles such as:

popin
gnomed
slide
slidefade


and named curves such as:

cinematic
snappy
smooth
soft_spring
snappy_spring


This general visual direction is good.

Do not introduce unsupported styles without checking Hyprland 0.56.x documentation.

Appearance goal

The visual direction is:

dark / glassy / futuristic / neon

Desired native effects include:

rounded corners
blur
aurora-style blur if supported
motion blur
restrained wobble
shadows
glow
Matugen colors

Important: previously I accidentally used unsupported wobble configuration keys. Do not repeat that mistake. Verify the exact Hyprland 0.56.2 option names/types first.

Hyprfocus

Hyprfocus is working.

The desired behavior is:

keyboard focus → shrink
mouse focus     → flash
floating windows → animated


Current verified configuration:

hl.config({
	plugin = {
		hyprfocus = {
			keyboard_focus_animation = "shrink",
			mouse_focus_animation = "flash",
			animate_floating = true,
		},
	},
})


Keep this separate from native animations.lua.

Other plugin

